{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793520002,"nonce":"CYuMHtIjTnLPPvOSq7aDp8k2W+4=","title":"Dogfood with real login: GitHub OAuth, identity and role stores, an admin and a member","message":"Owner 2026-11-01, testing dogfood (just up dogfood, kind): the Account page shows 'This server is running without the identity store, so there are no linked accounts to show' and the access page shows 'This deployment has no role store — authorization is off (dev), so there is nobody to grant anything to'. Owner: 'Ideally we should enroll an admin and a member'. Do after the one-kind-cluster stack (#65-#68) lands.\n\nWhy: dogfood is the staging env (owner 2026-11-01). It runs scarab.devInsecure=true, as the old colima dogfood did: no login, every caller is Owner, no identity store (ADR-0069 linked accounts), no role store (RBAC). Staging should run the login and authorization a real install runs.\n\nProposed:\n1. GitHub OAuth through the existing GitHub App 4323648 (a GitHub App has its own OAuth client id; the owner generates a client secret in the App settings and puts it in ~/.config/scarab/dogfood.env as SCARAB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET). Chart values scarab.oauth.{clientId,authorizeUrl,tokenUrl,userinfoUrl,scopes,owners}; secret via secrets.existingSecret / oauthClientSecret. The chart refuses oauth together with devInsecure, so dogfood drops devInsecure (also closes 'every local visitor is Owner').\n2. Callback URL: check how the server builds redirect_uri (public_url or request host). If from public_url, the callback would hit dogfood-scarab.ahiravan.dev, where the Cloudflare path rule allows only ^/webhooks/: either use a localhost callback (http://127.0.0.1:\u003cport\u003e/…, GitHub allows it) or add the callback path to the dashboard rule. just up dogfood's outside probe must keep checking that nothing else is public.\n3. Enroll an ADMIN and a MEMBER: admin = github:thulasi-ram through scarab.oauth.owners (bootstrap Owner); member = a second GitHub account the owner picks, granted the member role on the dogfood org through the role store API after its first login (seeded by up.sh when the id is in dogfood.env, e.g. DOGFOOD_MEMBER=github:\u003clogin\u003e). Show both on the access page; the member must be refused admin actions (a quick check in the recipe or a documented manual test).\n4. Step-up (ADR-0073): admins without a passkey are reported at boot; decide whether dogfood enrolls a passkey for the admin or documents the warning.\n5. Later, separately: Dex in-cluster as an OIDC provider for just e2e, if login flows need e2e coverage with no external dependency (not needed for staging).\n\nAcceptance: just up dogfood boots without devInsecure; logging in at the local UI as the owner shows the linked GitHub identity on the Account page; the access page lists the admin and the member; the member is refused an admin-only action; the outside probe still finds only /webhooks/ public; no secret printed or committed.","files":null}]}